# mws meta workspace

`{{.ProjectName}}/` is a **meta workspace** managed by [`mws`](https://github.com/sustinbebustin/mws). This file covers the workspace layout and how to work inside it; the project itself is described in the `CLAUDE.md` of your working copy, which loads alongside this one.

## Where you are

Working dir = one **working copy**: the project's native repos as direct children, plus harness symlinks. Peer copies are siblings inside the meta workspace (`main/`, feature copies, ...), each with its own independent checkouts and env files, so work in one copy never touches another's git state. If your cwd is the meta root itself, you are outside every copy; code work happens inside one.

Shared vs copy-local:

- **Shared (harness)** -- every entry in `<meta>/.mws/` (`CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/`, `.workspace/`, `justfile`, ...) is symlinked into every copy. Editing one through a copy edits it for all copies.
- **Copy-local** -- the native repos, env files, `.scratch/`, and any file created in the copy that has not been promoted.

Reference paths relative to the current dir, never absolute paths into a copy: a peer copy sits at a different path.

Worktrees of a copy live at `<copy>/.wt/<name>/` (`mws wt new <name>`); use the `mws` skill.

```
{{.ProjectName}}/            # meta root: git repo for harness + config only
├── .mws.toml          # mws config: repos, env mappings, setup commands, ports
├── .mws/              # harness; every entry symlinks into every working copy
├── .envs/             # env staging, copied into new copies (untracked)
├── .trash/            # copies removed by `mws rm` (untracked)
└── <copy>/            # a working copy (untracked); not a git repo at the top level
    ├── <repo>/        # native repo: own .git/, own branch
    ├── .scratch/      # copy-local in-flight work
    ├── .mws-ports.env # port lease, once the copy claims a slot (generated; never edit)
    ├── .wt/<name>/    # worktrees of this copy
    └── CLAUDE.md .claude/ .workspace/ ...  # symlinks into <meta>/.mws/
```

## Git

- Code: commit inside the native repo, `git -C <repo> ...`.
- Harness and config: the meta root (nearest ancestor holding `.mws.toml`) is the repo, and `mws init` already committed it. Commit later changes with `git -C <meta> add .gitignore .mws.toml .mws README.md CLAUDE.md && git -C <meta> commit`.

## mws commands

```bash
mws ls                         # working copies of this meta workspace, with their ports
mws path [copy]                # absolute path of a working copy
mws clone <name>               # new peer working copy: clones repos, renders env files, runs setup commands
mws rm <copy>                  # move a copy to .trash/ (mws restore <copy> undoes it)
mws promote <path>             # move a copy-local file into the harness, symlink it into every copy
mws relink                     # re-create harness symlinks in every copy
mws env sync [copy]            # re-render a copy's env files from staging
mws env stage [copy]           # capture a copy's env files into staging
mws env diff [copy]            # compare a copy's env files with staging
mws ports [copy]               # a copy's port slot and exported variables
mws ports claim|release [copy] # give a copy its own port slot, or put it back on the defaults
mws wt new|ls|rm|path <name>   # worktrees of the current copy
```
